u_{X'}:X'_{\mathrm{proet}}	o X_{\mathrm{et}}$ are the same morphism of sites $g$, given by $U\mapsto X'	imes_XU$ with the chosen fibre products [def-weil-proetale-inverse-image, def-weil-pbc-inverse-image, def-weil-pbc-site-comparison-morphism]. By [lem-weil-pbc-site-cohomology-pullback](4), $v_{\mathrm{proet}}^*
u_X^*=H^1(c_1^{-1})g^*$ and $
u_{X'}^*v_{\mathrm{et}}^*=H^1(c_2^{-1})g^*$, where $c_1:v_{\mathrm{proet}}^{-1}
u_X^{-1}\cong g^{-1}$ and $c_2:
u_{X'}^{-1}v_{\mathrm{et}}^{-1}\cong g^{-1}$ are compatible with the units. With coefficient naturality (2),
$$H^1(d)v_{\mathrm{proet}}^*C_X=H^1(d\,v_{\mathrm{proet}}^{-1}\sigma_X\,c_1^{-1})g^*,\qquad C_{X'}H^1(e)v_{\mathrm{et}}^*=H^1(\sigma_{X'}
u_{X'}^{-1}(e)\,c_2^{-1})g^*.$$
The two sheaf maps $g^{-1}L_X^{\mathrm{et}}	o L_{X'}^{\mathrm{pro}}$ agree: a map out of $g^{-1}$ is determined by its composite with the unit of $g$, which $c_1,c_2$ carry to the composite units, and on a local tensor $z\otimes a$ over an etale $U	o X$ both composites give $v^\sharp(z)\otimes a$ over $X'	imes_XU$, by the unit formula for $\sigma$ in [lem-amb-finite-root-site-comparison], the root-tensor pullback $e$ of [lem-asd-etale-finite-twist-pullback] and the formula for $d$. Local tensors generate the sheafified tensor [def-pur-sheaf-tensor-product]. Hence $H^1(d)v_{\mathrm{proet}}^*C_X=C_{X'}H^1(e)v_{\mathrm{et}}^*$, the geometric compatibility of the coefficient comparison. Substituting $\kappa_X^{\mathrm{et}}(u)$ and Steps 3 and 4 gives $H^1(d)v_{\mathrm{proet}}^*\kappa_X^{\mathrm{pro}}(u)=\kappa_{X'}^{\mathrm{pro}}(v^*u)$. The pro-etale coefficient square $d\,v_{\mathrm{proet}}^{-1}(\varphi_X^{\mathrm{pro}})=\varphi_{X'}^{\mathrm{pro}}a^{\mathrm{pro}}$, with $a^{\mathrm{pro}}:v_{\mathrm{proet}}^{-1}\mu^{\mathrm{pro}}_{m,X}	o\mu^{\mathrm{pro}}_{m,X'}$ the root map adjoint to pullback of units, holds since both send a local root to its pulled-back root tensored with $1_A$; identities and composites are respected by the same unit argument.
